From 0b8731b5d64fc8d3dd1521b994e2a4b36d08ed55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moritz Angermann <moritz.angermann@iohk.io>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:07:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Model B: drive the v3 bytecode VM for hydra/flake jobsets
 (behind NIX_V3_DIRECT_EVAL)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wire nix-eval-jobs' worker to the v3-native accessor surface (nix-expr-v3)
so v3 owns the heavy eval while all store-side logic stays byte-identical.

Gate: NIX_V3_DIRECT_EVAL engages v3 for hydra's --expr getFlake shape (and
--flake without lock overrides); legacy jobsets and --apply stay on TW.
Per-job TW routing (jobNeedsTreeWalker): aggregate/functor/lambda jobs.

TW-RETRY SAFETY NET (round-2 review CR7-R1/CR8-R1): v3 is the fast path,
the tree-walker is the correctness oracle.  On ANY per-job v3 exception the
worker rebuilds the handle and RETRIES that job on the tree-walker (unless
NIX_V3_REQUIRE), so a v3-vs-TW divergence can never make hydra wrong or
worse-formatted — worst case a divergent job is evaluated twice.  This
subsumes the numeric-segment / CA-output / non-attrset-meta / output-shape
/ error-byte divergence classes.

Also: CallDepthError -> fatal Response::Error (TW StackOverflowError
parity); engagement requires empty applyExpr (CR6-D4); v3Require read once.

git-am-clean on pristine v2.34.1 (65ebf5b).  Gates: shadow parity 10 jobs
v3==TW (3 retries all -> correct), full --brute 41/41 on the v3 nix.

